    "abstract": "Illustrated parts figure for the datalink router installation in the forward avionics rack, showing the display unit, the router assembly, the data concentrators and the satellite data unit across the three released standards.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "To identify the parts of the datalink router installation in the forward avionics rack, including the items that differ between the first and second router standards.",
      "figure_note": "The figure is drawn from the forward avionics bay looking aft with the rack door removed. Sheet 1 shows the rack elevation and sheet 2 the outboard shelf. Item 10 and item 10A are the display unit at the second and first standards respectively. The part number is the same for both, which is why they were listed as one item until this issue and why a station had no way of telling them apart. They are distinguished only by the hardware modification letter stamped after the serial number on the unit label, on the left-hand side of the front face: letter C or later is item 10, letters A and B are item 10A. A unit whose label is illegible or absent is treated as item 10A and is not fitted to an aircraft at the second standard. The second data concentrator at item 40 is present only on aircraft at the second standard. The satellite data unit at item 50 is fitted at the second standard and is replaced by a variant at the third standard, which is not yet in production. The antenna feed cable to the aft position is not shown on this figure."
    },
